<title>MOROCCO: Morocco and Germany to build seaside resort.</title>
<headline>Morocco and Germany to build seaside resort.</headline>
<dateline>RABAT 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Moroccan and German hotel groups have signed an agreement to build a 200 million dirham ($21.7 million) seaside resort in the southern Moroccan city of Agadir, Moroccan news agency MAP said on Thursday.</p>
<p>MAP said the accord was signed between German operator Touristik Union International (TUI) and the Moroccan-German group Iberotel-Maroc on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The complex will be operational in 1999. It will have 700 beds and generate 3,000 jobs.</p>
</text>
